Package: arwad
Type: Package
Title: Compile Loop-Heavy R Functions to Native Code Through 'Goose'
Version: 0.0.0.9011
Authors@R:
    person("Bashar", "Al Agha", email = "ba8160@srmist.edu.in",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-5178-2345"))
Description: Compiles R functions written in a statistical subset of the
    language (scalar and vector arithmetic, loops, indexing) to native code
    through the 'Goose' language and a C compiler, and calls the result from
    R. Results must match GNU R: any situation the native path does not model
    (an error, a warning, an unusual index) is handed back to GNU R, which
    re-runs the call. Functions outside the subset are returned unchanged
    with the reason recorded.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/bashar-al-agha/arwad
BugReports: https://github.com/bashar-al-agha/arwad/issues
Depends:
    R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports:
    stats,
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
    seminr,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
SystemRequirements: Goose (>= 2026.3) <https://github.com/aardappel/goose>
    for compilation, and the C compiler R uses for packages (Rtools on
    Windows). Without them every function runs in GNU R.
Config/testthat/edition: 3
